{"name":"Raw Garnet Viola","hex":"#8b6c7e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"raw","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Rawang."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Not cooked. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Subsisting on, or pertaining to, a diet of raw food."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raw"},{"term":"garnet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard transparent mineral that is often used as gemstones and abrasives.","A dark red color, like that of the gemstone."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark red colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garnet"},{"term":"viola","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several flowering plants, of the genus Viola, including the violets and pansies."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bowed  tenor instrument larger than a violin but smaller than a cello, used in orchestras and string quartets.","An organ stop with a similar tone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/viola"}],"entries":[{"title":"Garnet","blocks":[{"text":"Garnets are a group of silicate minerals that have been used since the Bronze Age as gemstones and abrasives."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Garnet_Andradite20.jpg/330px-Garnet_Andradite20.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garnet"},{"title":"Viola","blocks":[{"text":"The viola ( vee-OH-lə, Italian: [ˈvjɔːla, viˈɔːla]) is a string instrument of the violin family, and is usually bowed when played. The viola is slightly larger than the violin and has a lower sound. Since the 18th century, it has been the middle or alto voice of the violin family, between the violin (which is tuned a perfect fifth higher) and the cello (which is tuned an octave lower). The strings from low to high are typically tuned to C3, G3, D4, and A4."}],"image":"